text.section:
The Department of Military Affairs shall support the objectives of the Governor and federal authorities by:

Administering and employing the Virginia Militia, as set forth in § 44-1;


Integrating into state operations all supporting Department of Defense capabilities and those forces provided by supporting states in a Title 32 or State Active Duty status;


Providing for the safety of citizens of the Commonwealth by maintaining order and public safety and assisting in counter-drug efforts, in cooperation with Virginia State Police and local law-enforcement agencies;


Preparing and executing contingency plans to provide for a timely and capable response to chemical, biological, radiological, nuclear, or explosive incidents;


Preparing and executing contingency plans necessary for the provision of homeland defense;


Ensuring the support to families of service members of the Virginia National Guard;


Administering a state at-risk program for youth; and


Recruiting a force sufficiently manned and trained to accomplish the above duties.
